::: {.callout-note appearance="simple" icon=false}
Text on this page is EPA's own published wording (a U.S. Government work, not
subject to domestic copyright), extracted from EPA's published indicator page
and verified paragraph by paragraph against the archived HTML. Data, chart
code, and the full extraction pipeline are maintained in the
[coastal-flooding](https://github.com/climateindicators/coastal-flooding)
repository, which this page reads its data from directly.

One change was made to EPA's wording. EPA draws Figure 1 as a map of small
bar graphs; this page draws the same data as one row per site, because the 42
sites cluster too tightly along the Mid-Atlantic coast to read on a map at this
size. The figure description says "This chart" and "Each row" where EPA's says
"This map" and "Each small bar graph."
:::

